        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Chaturanga (Sanskrit: \"four-armed,\" referring to the four divisions of the Indian army) appears in the Gupta Empire period (~600 CE), though some researchers argue for origins 200+ years earlier. The Harshacharita (~625 CE) is among the earliest textual references."
    },
