        "title": "Chess - From Chaturanga to AlphaZero",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "When the Sassanid Empire (Persia) absorbed the game from India in the 6th-7th centuries CE, it became Shatranj (from Sanskrit \"chaturanga\" via sound change). The Islamic conquest of Persia spread Shatranj across the entire Arab world by the 9th century."
